            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WLS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is very good. The flavors are spot on. Just make sure you use a good quality balsamic that isn't too old!! I have added a few fresh herbs from my garden on occasion for a different twist. Either way, a lovely way to bring some fresh juicy flavors to any meal of the day!",
            "datePublished": "2019-07-12T11:51:40.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alesa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think this was just okay. I had half of a watermelon in the fridge and this was a simple enough salad to make for lunch. I made this subbing 1/2 packet of Stevia for the Sweet 'n Low. I followed the rest of the recipe, as listed, reducing by one half. I think next time I will try the salad with less balsamic vinegar, or by subbing apple cider vinegar. I had to add quite a bit of salt to my serving to enhance the flavor. Overall, it was a refreshing change from the usual tomato-cucumber-onion salad.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-14T23:08:10.833Z"
          },
